<div class="calcpad-output">
 <!-- Mixes Markdown headings, lists and tables with Calcpad math using `#markdown` blocks and `#md on`, the building block for Markdown-driven reports. -->
 <h1>Markdown in CalcpadCE</h1>
 <hr/>
 <h3>Heading 3</h3>
 <h4>Heading 4</h4>
 <h5>Heading 5</h5>
 <h6>Heading 6</h6>
 <p>A quote in comment can be escaped by entering 'another' one</p>
 <p>
  This text is
  <strong>bold</strong>
  , this is
  <em>italic</em>
  and this is
  <em>
   <strong>bold-italic</strong>
  </em>
  .
You can also have
  <ins>underlined</ins>
  ,
  <del>deleted</del>
  and ≡marked≡ text.
Adding
  <sub>sub</sub>
  script and
  <sup>super</sup>
  script is now easier than ever.
Code:
  <code>c = a + b</code>
  Image:
  <img alt="CalcpadCE" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/imartincei/CalcpadCE/refs/heads/main/docs/media/logo.svg"/>
  Links:
  <a href="https://www.markdownguide.org">https://www.markdownguide.org</a>
  ,
  <a href="https://calcpad-ce.org">CalcpadCE website</a>
 </p>
 <blockquote>
  <p>Blockquote</p>
  <blockquote>
   <p>Next level</p>
  </blockquote>
 </blockquote>
</div>
